  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be two distinct solutions of the differential equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;respectively. Then, the number of points of intersection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is",
    "image": null
  },
